# No trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY called node_modules and nothing else. A
# symlink called node_modules — which is what a linked local dependency is, and
# what several package managers create — is not a directory, so the pattern
# misses it and the link gets committed. That has happened elsewhere in this
# workspace once already: a symlink pointing at its own parent went into a
# commit, and every checkout afterwards failed with ELOOP.
node_modules

# There is no build. `run.sh` runs Vite and the page is generated by middleware,
# so there is no `index.html` for a bundler to start from and nothing that would
# serve the output if there were. This line is here so that an experiment does
# not leave a second answer to "what does this page say" in the repository.
dist

# This app keeps nothing. It holds a few hundred kilobytes of somebody else's
# file in memory for as long as a container is looking at it, and forgets it
# when the page closes — no cache, no index, no recently-opened list. If a
# directory ever appears here holding something read out of a user's
# filesystem, that is a bug and not a feature that needs a line in this file.
.DS_Store
